+## Acceptance
+
+- A `/implement` run whose review panel accepts a `### FINDING_N: [OUT_OF_SCOPE]` finding — or a scope-drift `OUT_OF_SCOPE_DRIFT` reclassification — files those OOS (non-zero `OOS filed`) instead of silently dropping them, on both the production review-core path (`tally-code-votes.sh` → `emit-tally.sh`) and the coder-skipped path (`review-and-fix.sh`).
+- `count_non_security` (Python `python/oos.py` + awk `oos-non-security-block-count.awk`) counts `[OUT_OF_SCOPE]`-tagged accepted blocks and still returns 0 for bare `### FINDING_N:` (no tag).
+- `emit-tally.sh` no longer overwrites or truncates the tally-written `oos-accepted-review.md` when `OOS_ACCEPTED_COUNT > 0` (both the `oos-serialize` and the missing-`oos.md` truncate branches are guarded).
+- Accepted OOS blocks in the dedicated OOS sinks carry canonical `### OOS_<seq>:` headers (no surviving `### FINDING_` header), produced by the shared `normalize-oos-block-header.sh` helper (line-1-only rewrite; body lines preserved).
+- Security-tagged OOS remain held locally and are never written to the public accepted-OOS sink.
+- New regression tests cover the legacy-header counting, the `emit-tally` preserve branch (with and without `oos.md`), the `review-and-fix` skipped-routing normalization, the dual-sink single-write guard, and both the bash (`test-oos-disposition-gate.sh`) and Python (`test_oos.py`) gates; `make lint` and `make py-test` pass.
